          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"U1\") (value \"TPS62933\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "U1 (TPS62933) bucks +24V → +5V"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The regulator is operated beyond its input rating and may fail or be damaged, preventing generation of the 5 V and 3.3 V rails.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["U1"],
      "pins": ["U1.2"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(U1-EN-Pad2)"],
      "observed": "The TPS62933 enable pin is explicitly marked no-connect.",
      "expected": "The enable pin should be driven to a valid high level or otherwise biased according to the TPS62933 datasheet so the regulator can start.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"136\") (name \"unconnected-(U1-EN-Pad2)\") ... (node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"EN\") (pintype \"input+no_connect\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "U1 (TPS62933) bucks +24V → +5V"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "With EN left floating, the buck may remain disabled, so the intended 5 V and downstream 3.3 V rails may not be produced.",
      "confidence": 0.94
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["T3", "R7", "D3"],
      "pins": ["T3.1", "T3.2", "T3.3", "R7.1", "R7.2", "D3.1", "D3.2"],
      "nets": ["/G_{RPP}", "/+24V_{F}", "+24V", "GND"],
      "observed": "T3 is a P-channel MOSFET in series between /+24V_{F} at its source and +24V at its drain. Its gate is connected through R7 (33 kΩ) to its source; D3 connects the gate to GND. At normal positive input voltage, this does not pull the P-channel gate below its source to turn it on.",
      "expected": "The reverse-polarity protection MOSFET should have a gate-bias network that turns it on with correctly polarized input while limiting its gate-to-source voltage.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"6\") (name \"/+24V_{F}\") ... (node (ref \"R7\") (pin \"2\") ...) (node (ref \"T3\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"S\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"3\") (name \"+24V\") ... (node (ref \"T3\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"D\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"47\") (name \"/G_{RPP}\") ... (node (ref \"D3\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"K\")) (node (ref \"R7\") (pin \"1\") ...) (node (ref \"T3\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"G\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R7\") (value \"33k\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "README states the PCB includes \"reverse polarity protection\""
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The series MOSFET is likely off under normal input polarity, interrupting the +24 V rail to the loads and regulator.",
      "confidence": 0.96
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomalies are present: the 24 V input is applied directly to a TPS62933, whose input rating is lower, and its enable pin is left unconnected. The series P-channel reverse-polarity MOSFET also appears biased off during normal operation."
}

